1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:06,328
A binary operation combines two elements of a set and must give an answer inside the same set.

2
00:00:06,328 --> 00:00:09,153
Addition on the natural numbers: yes.

3
00:00:09,153 --> 00:00:13,359
Subtraction: no, three minus five escapes.

4
00:00:13,359 --> 00:00:16,614
Multiplication on the integers: yes.

5
00:00:16,614 --> 00:00:20,859
Division: no, one over two is not an integer.

6
00:00:20,859 --> 00:00:23,203
One counter example is enough.

